From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:36:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 074/131] arm64: dts: a22x: CPU idle states and the SoC system
 timer

The stock idle states are "mediatek,idle-state", which the PSCI cpuidle
driver ignores, so the CPUs only executed WFI. Mark the CPU-off and
cluster-off states "arm,idle-state" and list only those per CPU
(mcusys-off and the s2idle state need SPM/MCUPM support). Add the system
timer at 0x10017000 (as on MT8192) for broadcast wakeups while a CPU's
arch timer is stopped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 44 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
index 67cd9e03e..554ffe06b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6833-samsung-a22x.dts
@@ -1686,3 +1686,47 @@ &consys {
 	memory-region = <&{/reserved-memory/wifi-reserve-memory}>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * CPU idle. The stock idle states are "mediatek,idle-state", which the PSCI
+ * cpuidle driver ignores, so the CPUs only ever did WFI. Enable the CPU-off
+ * and cluster-off states (handled by ATF alone, as on MT8192); mcusys-off
+ * and the s2idle state need the SPM/MCUPM side and stay unused for now.
+ */
+&cpuoff_l {
+	compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+};
+
+&cpuoff_b {
+	compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+};
+
+&clusteroff_l {
+	compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+};
+
+&clusteroff_b {
+	compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+};
+
+&{/cpus/cpu@000} { cpu-idle-states = <&cpuoff_l &clusteroff_l>; };
+&{/cpus/cpu@001} { cpu-idle-states = <&cpuoff_l &clusteroff_l>; };
+&{/cpus/cpu@002} { cpu-idle-states = <&cpuoff_l &clusteroff_l>; };
+&{/cpus/cpu@003} { cpu-idle-states = <&cpuoff_l &clusteroff_l>; };
+&{/cpus/cpu@004} { cpu-idle-states = <&cpuoff_l &clusteroff_l>; };
+&{/cpus/cpu@005} { cpu-idle-states = <&cpuoff_l &clusteroff_l>; };
+&{/cpus/cpu@100} { cpu-idle-states = <&cpuoff_b &clusteroff_b>; };
+&{/cpus/cpu@101} { cpu-idle-states = <&cpuoff_b &clusteroff_b>; };
+
+/ {
+	/*
+	 * SoC system timer: keeps running while a CPU's arch timer is off in
+	 * an idle state (broadcast wakeups; else only bc_hrtimer is there).
+	 */
+	timer@10017000 {
+		compatible = "mediatek,mt6833-timer", "mediatek,mt6765-timer";
+		reg = <0 0x10017000 0 0x1000>;
+		interrupts = <0 233 4>;
+		clocks = <&clk13m>;
+	};
+};
